.\" Man page of ninesql (P6-A). Plain man(7) macros; check with: man -l packaging/linux/ninesql.1
.TH NINESQL 1 "2026-11-19" "NineSQL" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ninesql \- native database client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ninesql
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ninesql
opens the NineSQL window: a database client for PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB, SQLite and
wire-compatible engines (TimescaleDB, YugabyteDB, QuestDB, TiDB), with a SQL editor, a results
grid, a database navigator, data editing, export and CSV import, and an import of DBeaver
workspaces that never modifies DBeaver's files.
.PP
It needs a Wayland or X11 session and a GPU with Vulkan 1.2 drivers.
.PP
NineSQL sends no telemetry and opens network connections only to the databases you declare and
their SSH hops.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Any other argument is refused (exit status 2).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ninesql/settings.toml
Preferences (default \fI~/.config/ninesql/\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/ninesql/workspace/
Projects, connections, connection types and scripts (default \fI~/.local/share/ninesql/\fR).
Connection files hold references to saved secrets, never the secrets.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/ninesql/vault.bin
The encrypted vault of saved passwords, when the desktop keyring is not used.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/ninesql/known_hosts
SSH host keys accepted in NineSQL.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/ninesql/
Query history (\fIhistory.sqlite\fR) and \fIsession.json\fR, the windows and script tabs
reopened at the next start, never editor text (default \fI~/.local/state/ninesql/\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/known_hosts
Read, with NineSQL's own file, to verify SSH host keys.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_STATE_HOME
Base directories of the files above.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for an unknown argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
The tutorials at
.UR https://github.com/Yil00/ninesql/tree/main/docs/tutorials
.UE .
